  "claim": "The species of animal which the town, a community that forms part of the Centre USD 397 district, was named after is Antilocapra americana.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Antelope, Kansas. Sentence: Antelope got its name from antelope grazing near where the first school was being built.\nPage: Pronghorn. Sentence: The pronghorn ( ) (\"Antilocapra americana\") is a species of artiodactyl mammal indigenous to interior western and central North America.\nPage: Pronghorn. Sentence: Though not an antelope, it is often known colloquially in North America as the American antelope, prong buck, pronghorn antelope, or simply antelope because it closely resembles the true antelopes of the Old World and fills a similar ecological niche due to parallel evolution.\nPage: Centre USD 397. Sentence: The district includes the communities of Lincolnville, Lost Springs, Pilsen, Tampa, Ramona, Antelope, Burdick, nearby rural areas of Marion / Morris / Dickinson / Chase Counties.",
